sequenceDiagram
    participant User as User / ODH Operator
    participant K8sAPI as Kubernetes API<br/>6443/TCP HTTPS TLS 1.2+
    participant Webhook as Webhook Server<br/>9443/TCP HTTPS TLS
    participant MRReconciler as ModelRegistry<br/>Reconciler
    participant REST as REST Deployment<br/>{registry-name}<br/>8080/TCP HTTP
    participant Proxy as kube-rbac-proxy<br/>8443/TCP HTTPS TLS
    participant Postgres as PostgreSQL<br/>5432/TCP
    participant Route as Route / HTTPRoute<br/>443/TCP HTTPS TLS
    participant Client as External Client

    rect rgb(230, 245, 255)
        Note over User,Route: Flow 1: ModelRegistry Instance Provisioning
        User->>K8sAPI: Create ModelRegistry CR<br/>HTTPS/6443, Bearer Token
        K8sAPI->>Webhook: Validate & Default<br/>HTTPS/9443, Kubernetes Admission
        Webhook-->>K8sAPI: Admission Response
        K8sAPI-->>MRReconciler: Watch Event (reconcile trigger)
        MRReconciler->>K8sAPI: Create REST Deployment<br/>+ kube-rbac-proxy sidecar<br/>HTTPS/6443, ServiceAccount
        MRReconciler->>K8sAPI: Create PostgreSQL Deployment<br/>HTTPS/6443, ServiceAccount
        MRReconciler->>K8sAPI: Create Services, Secrets<br/>(TLS certs, DB credentials)<br/>HTTPS/6443, ServiceAccount
        MRReconciler->>K8sAPI: Create RBAC Resources<br/>(Role, RoleBinding, Groups)<br/>HTTPS/6443, ServiceAccount
        MRReconciler->>K8sAPI: Create NetworkPolicy<br/>HTTPS/6443, ServiceAccount
        MRReconciler->>K8sAPI: Create Route/HTTPRoute<br/>HTTPS/6443, ServiceAccount
        MRReconciler->>K8sAPI: Update ModelRegistry Status<br/>HTTPS/6443, ServiceAccount
    end

    rect rgb(255, 245, 230)
        Note over Client,Postgres: Flow 2: Registry API Access
        Client->>Route: REST API Request<br/>HTTPS/443, TLS
        Route->>Proxy: Forward to kube-rbac-proxy<br/>HTTPS/8443
        Proxy->>K8sAPI: TokenReview<br/>HTTPS/6443, TLS 1.2+
        K8sAPI-->>Proxy: Token Valid
        Proxy->>K8sAPI: SubjectAccessReview<br/>(registry-user-{name} Role)<br/>HTTPS/6443, TLS 1.2+
        K8sAPI-->>Proxy: Access Granted
        Proxy->>REST: Proxied Request<br/>HTTP/8080, Proxy-authenticated
        REST->>Postgres: Query Model Metadata<br/>5432/TCP, DB Credentials
        Postgres-->>REST: Query Results
        REST-->>Proxy: Response
        Proxy-->>Route: HTTPS Response
        Route-->>Client: JSON Response
    end
